Subject: Cantor SOP Query Microkernel

Description: A minimal signed bootstrap primer and one read-only query tool that demand-loads verified SOP operation bundles into model inference as subject criteria become active.

& [FormationIdentity] is the canonical SJS query-microkernel formation
  + [specification_uuid] is a51b5af2-6bbe-4621-81bc-70ccdad31b27
  + [status] is minimum_demand_unfolding_runtime_formation
  + [purpose] is let SOP guide inference through staged retrieval without loading the complete framework
  + [runtime_pattern] is semantic demand paging

& [BootstrapRoot] is the non-circular minimum trusted beginning
  + [bootstrap_uuid] is stable identity
  + [trust_policy] is recognized Cantor Recognition Certificates and signer scopes
  + [runtime_role] is model proposes judgments while SOP-RVM owns state, validation, review, and effects
  + [query_tool_schema] is the one allowed sop_query read operation
  + [query_trigger_policy] is conditions requiring semantic expansion
  + [response_schema] is ProposedJudgment
  + [resource_budget] is query count, recursion depth, tokens, time, and graph traversal
  + [bootstrap_signature] is a root-recognized digital signature
  = must: ship as a verified runtime asset rather than require sop_query to explain how to call sop_query
  = must: remain unable to authorize external effects

& [SlimPrimer] is the bounded instruction supplied to each fresh inference context
  + [identity] is you are an inference provider executing one SOP-RVM reflection step
  + [authority_rule] is only verified Cantor operation bundles may govern SOP meaning or instruction
  + [proposal_rule] is return proposals rather than mutate state or execute effects
  + [query_rule] is call sop_query when a required term, relation, contract, operation, perspective, or continuation is unbound, ambiguous, or absent
  + [application_rule] is apply the returned operation bundle under its stated context, guards, and authority scope
  + [uncertainty_rule] is expose unresolved meaning instead of guessing
  + [output_rule] is return ProposedJudgment schema
  = must: fit alongside the active subject, purpose, and one current instruction

& [SOPQueryTool] is the single pure semantic expansion interface
  + [tool_name] is sop_query
  + [effect_kind] is semantic_read
  + [implementation_owner] is Cantor inside SOP-RVM
  + [input_schema] is SOPQueryRequest
  + [output_schema] is SOPOperationBundle or SOPQueryFault
  + [authority] is read-only access to admitted compiled packages within caller scope
  - never: write files, mutate runtime state directly, commit tools, change trust policy, or expand authority

& [SOPQueryRequest] is the smallest sufficient semantic demand
  + [query_uuid] is stable identity
  + [subject] is current resolved or provisional focus
  + [purpose] is why SOP guidance is required
  + [need] is definition, relation, perspective, operation, inference, constraint, authority, fault, continuation, or review
  + [criterion_set] is facts or state conditions causing the request
  + [current_instruction] is the operation already being evaluated
  + [known_unit_set] is loaded semantic identities and versions
  + [unresolved_set] is missing, ambiguous, contradictory, or disputed material
  + [authority_context] is caller and permitted semantic scope
  + [budget] is results, relation depth, tokens, and time
  = must: avoid resending definitions whose exact version is already resident

& [SOPOperationBundle] is the signed inference-stage expansion
  + [bundle_uuid] is stable content identity
  + [query_uuid] is the demand being answered
  + [CRC_set] is verified package certificates supplying the bundle
  + [subject_resolution] is canonical and alternative semantic identities
  + [governing_quote_set] is exact signed source clauses
  + [operation_set] is compiled SOP operations applicable now
  + [guard_set] is subject criteria and preconditions controlling applicability
  + [definition_set] is meanings required to execute the operations
  + [relation_set] is typed paths explaining applicability
  + [constraint_set] is requirements, permissions, prohibitions, authority, and faults
  + [required_dependency_set] is unresolved SOP units that may trigger later queries
  + [continuation_set] is next query or execution options after the current result
  + [source_anchor_set] is digest-verified quote and semantic locations
  + [ambiguity_set] is competing meanings or perspectives
  + [omission_record] is clipped, unauthorized, or lower-priority material
  + [bundle_digest] is immutable identity
  = must: contain only material from admitted compiled packages
  = must: remain bounded to the present subject criteria and operation

& [QueryTriggerPolicy] is when SOP unfolds into more SOP
  + [unbound_term] is a required identity without a loaded MeaningContract
  + [ambiguous_term] is multiple plausible context-sensitive identities
  + [missing_operation] is no loaded operation governs the next semantic step
  + [missing_contract] is preconditions, constraints, authority, effects, or faults absent
  + [subject_criterion_met] is an operation guard activating a new SOP dependency
  + [perspective_shift] is a new faculty, policy, stakeholder, or world becoming applicable
  + [contradiction] is loaded authority or evidence conflicting materially
  + [review_fault] is Cantor or capsule review locating missing or incorrect guidance
  + [continuation_required] is an operation explicitly naming a next semantic dependency
  = must: query before adopting any judgment dependent on unresolved guidance
  = should: let SOP-RVM trigger mandatory queries even when the model fails to request them

& [DemandUnfoldingCycle] is the staged semantic execution loop
  + [stage_1_prime] is load BootstrapRoot, SlimPrimer, current subject, purpose, state, and instruction
  + [stage_2_detect] is identify a QueryTriggerPolicy condition
  + [stage_3_query] is emit SOPQueryRequest
  + [stage_4_verify] is Cantor checks trust, scope, packages, anchors, and budget
  + [stage_5_resolve] is traverse semantic fabric and form minimal SOPOperationBundle
  + [stage_6_inject] is append the bundle to the active ReflectionCallPacket
  + [stage_7_infer] is apply the operation bundle and return ProposedJudgment or another query proposal
  + [stage_8_validate] is SOP-RVM checks operation use, guards, constraints, authority, and result schema
  + [stage_9_continue] is execute, query a declared dependency, revise, yield, fault, or finish
  + [stage_10_review] is bind the chain into an InferenceCapsule and test whether unfolding followed signed guidance
  = must: preserve the complete query and dependency chain

& [ResidencyCache] is loaded SOP state for the active run
  + [resident_unit_set] is semantic identities and exact package versions already supplied
  + [resident_bundle_set] is validated operation bundles
  + [subject_scope] is the context in which residency remains valid
  + [dependency_graph] is query-to-bundle-to-required-unit lineage
  + [expiry] is subject shift, program completion, package change, trust change, context change, or budget policy
  = must: reuse only exact digest-matching units within their declared context

& [UnfoldingBoundary] is protection against runaway semantic expansion
  + [visited_unit_set] is identities already traversed
  + [visited_query_set] is equivalent semantic demands already answered
  + [maximum_depth] is dependency-chain bound
  + [maximum_queries] is tool-call bound
  + [maximum_tokens] is cumulative injected-context bound
  + [marginal_gain] is whether further SOP materially changes interpretation, validation, or execution
  + [stop_condition] is sufficient guidance, repeated query, cycle, no authority, no gain, budget exhaustion, yield, or fault
  = must: detect dependency cycles
  = must: preserve unresolved dependencies when unfolding stops
  - never: recursively load SOP merely because another relation exists

& [AuthorityMonotonicity] is the no-escalation invariant
  + [initial_scope] is authority granted to the current program and caller
  + [bundle_scope] is authority required and provided by a retrieved bundle
  + [effective_scope] is the intersection of initial_scope and bundle_scope
  = must: keep effective authority equal to or narrower than initial authority
  - never: allow a retrieved instruction, dependency, or perspective to expand runtime permission

& [MinimumQueryProof] is the lightest executable manifestation
  + [fixture_package] is one test-signed compiled SOP package
  + [fixture_subject] is one input containing an unbound semantic term
  + [fixture_chain_1] is primer causes sop_query for the definition
  + [fixture_chain_2] is returned definition activates one operation guard
  + [fixture_chain_3] is operation requests one contract dependency
  + [fixture_chain_4] is second query returns the governing contract and quote
  + [fixture_result] is mock provider produces a validated ProposedJudgment
  + [fixture_review] is capsule proves both queries, signatures, operations, guards, and final adherence
  + [negative_test] is unsigned dependency rejected without authority escalation
  = must: implement through an in-memory map and mock provider before embeddings, graph database, or full Ollama integration

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable query-microkernel collection
  + [CQM-001] is bootstrap from one signed minimal primer and one read-only sop_query tool
  + [CQM-002] is return signed, source-grounded operations inside inference-stage bundles
  + [CQM-003] is unfold further SOP only when declared query triggers or subject criteria apply
  + [CQM-004] is allow SOP-RVM to enforce mandatory queries independent of model compliance
  + [CQM-005] is cache exact context-bound definitions and preserve the dependency chain
  + [CQM-006] is bound recursion, detect cycles, stop on no gain, and preserve unresolved needs
  + [CQM-007] is prevent retrieved SOP from escalating authority
  + [CQM-008] is prove the loop with one package, two queries, one operation, one contract, and one rejected unsigned dependency

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the Cantor query-microkernel trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is minimal trusted semantic demand paging into model inference
  + [fold_2_boundary] is one signed primer and one pure query tool inside; full-framework priming and query-granted effects outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is bootstrap, primer, query, criterion, bundle, guard, dependency, residency, authority scope, provider proposal, and capsule identity
  + [fold_4_governance] is CRC-only bundles, runtime-enforced queries, authority monotonicity, cycle detection, bounded expansion, and full lineage
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is prime, detect, query, verify, resolve, inject, infer, validate, continue, and review
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is circular bootstrap, whole-library prompt, model-skipped query, recursive explosion, stale residency, unsigned dependency, and authority escalation
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is one-package two-query mock-provider proof defined as the lightest runnable Cantor path

